Source provenance
=================

generator.c adapts OpenBSD lib/libc/crypt/arc4random.c revision 1.58
(2022-07-31). chacha.c adapts lib/libc/crypt/chacha_private.h revision 1.3
(2022-02-28), based on chacha-merged.c version 20080118 by D. J. Bernstein.
Both references are pinned to OpenBSD src commit:

  be1d1982dd83d04eb51a63726cd066959e1d1907

  https://github.com/openbsd/src/blob/be1d1982dd83d04eb51a63726cd066959e1d1907/lib/libc/crypt/arc4random.c
  https://github.com/openbsd/src/blob/be1d1982dd83d04eb51a63726cd066959e1d1907/lib/libc/crypt/chacha_private.h

Local adaptation retains the 20-round ChaCha core, original 64-bit counter and
eight-byte nonce layout, 1024-byte refill, 40-byte reserved key/nonce, seed XOR,
immediate reinitialization, and private randomized 1-2 MiB output budget.
It uses explicit BSP-owned state rather than libc allocation/locking/fork hooks,
separates seed collection from generation, exposes one-block generation for
manual debugger qualification, and adds compiler-resistant erasure and the
accepted 60-second reseed trigger. The core supports only the 256-bit key and
keystream generation needed by this construction; message XOR and 128-bit key
support are omitted. No upstream download is needed at build time.

